# Gyoza Maison — v0.7.0

*August 18, 2026*

Pre-production build of the Gyoza Maison online shop: the customer-facing storefront and the admin back office are both functional end to end.

## Storefront

- **Catalog**: gyoza listings with product detail (photo, description, meat/veggie category tags), stock availability, and pack size selection via a pack picker.
- **Cart & checkout**: add-to-cart from product cards, cart panel and floating cart button on mobile, checkout form (customer details with validation), and order confirmation.
- **Content pages**: home, "Our Gyozas", "About Us" (team introduction), and contact.
- **Navigation**: navbar with account access, dedicated mobile bottom navigation, layout with a footer pinned to the bottom of the screen.
- **Design system**: reusable components (buttons, badges, product/recipe cards, navbar, footer, cart) on a consistent visual language (dark background, coral accent).

## Admin back office

- **Authentication**: dedicated admin login (`/admin/login`) protecting all management pages.
- **Stock management**: product creation and stock quantity adjustments.
- **Order management**: order tracking with status filtering (reserved, preparing, ready, delivered, cancelled), controlled status transitions, pagination, and a preparation summary (quantities to prepare per product/pack).
- **Analytics**: dashboard with key metrics and a sales time series over a given period.

## Backend & infrastructure

- Spring Boot REST API (products, packs, orders, authentication, analytics) backed by PostgreSQL.
- Angular frontend with server-side rendering (SSR).
- Dockerized dev environment (`docker-compose.dev.yml`) and production configuration (`docker-compose.prod.yml`).
- Demo dataset seeded automatically on startup.

## Remaining before v1.0.0

- Test coverage (frontend and backend).
- Automated deployment (CI/CD).
